# Motion Studio Project Rules

> Manual rule (`@project`). Cursor already applies the root `AGENTS.md` to every request, and it carries the same generated NEVER/ALWAYS.

Local brief-to-video tool. Node 22+ ESM, no framework, no build step. `node:http` server on 127.0.0.1:4780, vanilla JS UI, GSAP templates rendered by headless Chrome (playwright-core) and ffmpeg, local TTS (Kokoro / Windows SAPI). Claude runs only inside Claude Code, started by a person (`/studio run`). No code path may call a model, except the four person-clicked paths, `server/director.mjs` (Run Director: the Claude seat, or the API worker in `server/worker/` on the person's own provider key), `server/generate.mjs` (Gemini assets with the person's own key), `server/voice-cloud.mjs` (ElevenLabs voice lines with the person's own key) and `server/assistant-model.mjs` (the Assistant panel's intent pick: one request to a connected API provider's model (never the Claude seat) with the person's own key for a line the parser does not know; the person still approves the card).

## Commands
- Install: `npm install` (Node 22.23.4+, 24.22.1+ or 26.12.1+, Chrome installed)
- UI: `npm run ui` → http://127.0.0.1:4780
- Engine: `node engine/cli.mjs help`
- Test: `npm test`

## Safety Rules (quick ref — full details: `.ai/docs/conventions.md`)

**Safety tiers**: the Claude/seat rules, the localhost-only server, secrets and child-process caps are the **Floor** (never override — ask the user instead). The other NEVER/ALWAYS items are **Guardrails** (can be consciously overridden with a documented reason).

### NEVER
<!-- BEGIN:NEVER (generated from conventions.md — do not edit) -->
- NEVER use `Math.random`, `Date.now`, `setTimeout` or `setInterval` to drive what a template shows → everything visible is a function of `seek(t)`
- NEVER invent a claim in a script → every on-screen claim traces to `source.json` bullets/facts via `source`
- NEVER let the director run `render`, `approve` or `sequence` → a person approves and renders in the UI. Approval is UI-only: `node engine/cli.mjs approve` refuses for everyone, and render needs that approval. Every agent asks the person before `render`, `approve` or `sequence` however it is started: Claude Code (`.claude/hooks/block-destructive.js`; inline `node -e` runs without a prompt, user decision 2026-10-29), Copilot (`.vscode/settings.json`) and Cursor (`.cursor/hooks/ask-before-render.js`)
- NEVER add an npm dependency or a framework for something Node's standard library does
- NEVER show non-English text in product chrome (UI labels, server errors, CLI output, template chrome) → video copy follows `brand.voice.lang`
**Security (NEVER — the Floor; never override, ask the user instead):**
- NEVER invoke Claude or any model from `server/`, the UI, the engine, a cron or a loop → one exception: `server/director.mjs`. A person clicks Run Director and the local server runs one of two Director backends, chosen once at click time and shown in the log: the Claude seat (Claude Code headless, `claude.exe -p "/studio run …"`, never a `.cmd` through a shell, on that person's own logged-in seat, with the `--allowedTools` allowlist in `config/studio.json` → `director` (never render or approve), `--permission-mode dontAsk`, `--max-turns`, a key-free child environment) or the API worker (`server/worker/`, only when `config/providers.json` → `default` names a provider whose `keyEnv` is set: a tool-calling loop over that provider's HTTP API with Node `fetch`, the key in a request header only, tools bound to one project and job that write only the draft files (source, script or outline), `fetch_page` on the brand's allowed hosts only, caps in `director.api`: turns, tokens, calls per day, timeouts, byte caps, `maxPrepareRounds`, `maxFetchesPerJob`, a pause file per provider on 429, no retry, no backend switch during a run). Both share a timeout of `jobTimeoutMinutes` × jobs, a capped log, one run at a time, a daily cap (`maxRunsPerDay`), and never render or approve. The second exception is `server/generate.mjs`: a person clicks Generate (or Refresh models) in the Brand tab; the local server makes one request to `generativelanguage.googleapis.com` with Node `fetch` and the person's own `GEMINI_API_KEY` (read from the environment variable named by `keyEnv`, never written, logged or sent to the UI, stripped from the Director child's environment together with every other `keyEnv`), capped by `config/studio.json` → `generate` (one request at a time, `maxImagesPerDay`, `maxImagesPerMonth`, `maxVideosPerDay`, `maxVideosPerMonth`, `maxRefreshesPerDay`, a timeout, response and download byte caps, a poll limit, a pause on 429), with model ids only from the list the person fetched or the first-run fallback, and saves one asset with `saveAsset` plus a `generated/<asset>.json` sidecar. An image or a clip (`gemini-omni-1.1-flash`) may carry 1-3 of the brand's own pictures as subject references; there is no batch: one click, one image or one clip. `engine/`, `engine/cli.mjs`, prepare, render and the Director have no path to it. The third exception is `server/voice-cloud.mjs` (user decision 2026-10-29): a person clicks Make cloud voice in a job's Script tab; the local server sends each missing voice line once to `api.elevenlabs.io` (`with-timestamps`) with Node `fetch` and the person's own key (the variable named by `config/studio.json` → `voiceCloud.keyEnv`, header only, redacted from every log), capped by `voiceCloud` (one run at a time, `maxLinesPerRun`, `maxLinesPerDay`, `maxCharsPerDay`, `maxCharsPerLine`, a timeout, a byte cap, a pause on 429 or a spent quota), and saves the audio and word times in `out/<project>/<job>/cloud-voice/`; prepare only reads them (`engine/cloudvoice.mjs`) and the Director has no path to it. The fourth exception is `server/assistant-model.mjs` (user decision 2026-10-30): a person sends a line in the Assistant panel with a model picked in its composer; the parser (`server/assistant.mjs`) runs first, a slash command or a line it knows never reaches a model, and only a line it does not know goes once to the picked model through the API worker's own adapters (`server/worker/adapters/`, one `pick_intent` tool) with Node `fetch` and the person's own key for that provider (the variable named by its `keyEnv`, header only, redacted from the log and every error; never the Claude seat), capped by `config/studio.json` → `assistant` (`freeform` on, `provider:model` refs from `models` only, chosen in the Settings tab from a provider's Connect list, `maxAsksPerDay`, one request at a time, a timeout, a byte cap, a pause on 429, no retry); the model names one of the panel's own intents with typed, capped args, which then go through the same proposal checks a typed line gets, and nothing is written until the person approves the card. The context it sends is ids and values (templates, job ids and states, video asset names, brand field names and current values), never a brief's text or a key. `/api/assistant/*` is never on the review link. The Settings tab's Connect (`server/worker/models.mjs`, user decision 2026-10-30) is one person-clicked request for an API provider's model list (metadata, no model runs; Gemini's goes through `refreshModels` in `server/generate.mjs`) with that provider's key in a header only, capped by `config/studio.json` → `settings` (`maxConnectsPerDay`, one at a time, a timeout, a byte cap, no retry); the list is saved under `logs/providers/`. No other call site, no auto-start, no retries
- NEVER reuse or extract the Claude Code CLI OAuth token, or proxy/share seat access → company seat; one abuse pattern cuts off the whole team
- NEVER use `--bare`, `--dangerously-skip-permissions` or any flag that disables auth or permission checks
- NEVER bind the UI server to anything but 127.0.0.1 or relax the Host / Origin / `X-Studio` checks → it is a local tool. One exception: the read-only review link (`npm run ui:review`, `server/review.mjs`), started by the person, bound to one private IPv4 of the machine (never 0.0.0.0), GET/HEAD only on a fixed allowlist (the normal UI flagged read-only, and the reads it needs), behind a random access code per start; it never runs the Director, Generate or TTS, never shows the Director log, and has no approve, render or any write
- NEVER put an API key or secret in a file → keys live in environment variables named by `keyEnv` in `config/providers.json`. One exception: the gitignored `.env` at the repo root, read by `server/keys.mjs` once at server start for the `keyEnv` names only (the environment wins; no value is logged, returned or stored), and written only by the Settings tab (`server/settings.mjs`, user decision 2026-10-30): `PUT|DELETE /api/settings/keys/<name>` on 127.0.0.1 with the Origin and `X-Studio` checks, a name from the `keyEnv` list only, a value of `[A-Za-z0-9._:+/=-]{8,512}`, one `NAME=` line rewritten through a temp file and a rename, the value set in the server's own environment and never returned, logged or shown again, a name the real environment sets left alone, never on the review link; never commit, copy, zip, print or read it any other way (the secret-file hooks stay)
- NEVER dump a secret file (`.env`, `*.local.md`, `*.local.json`, `*.pem`, `*.key`) with `cat`/`head`/`cp` → use the Read tool for the one value you need
- NEVER commit or share a file holding a key, token or password → stage explicit paths, never `git add -A`
- NEVER `spawn` with `shell: true` or a command string → `spawn(cmd, [args], { shell: false, windowsHide: true })` only
- NEVER start a child process without a timeout and a capped log → see `runEngine` in `server/server.mjs` and `config/studio.json` → `engine`
- NEVER build a path from an outside id or file name with `path.join` → `assertId` / `assertFileName` + `within()`
- NEVER write brief, brand or script text into composition HTML unescaped → `escapeHtml`; JSON into `<script>` → `jsonForScript`
- NEVER fetch a brief URL whose host is not in the brand's `sources.allowedHosts`
<!-- END:NEVER -->

### ALWAYS
<!-- BEGIN:ALWAYS (generated from conventions.md — do not edit) -->
- ALWAYS throw `StudioError(message, httpCode)` for expected failures → the server maps it to a JSON `{ error }` with that code
- ALWAYS write state with `writeJson` (atomic temp + rename) and read with `readJson(file, fallback)`
- ALWAYS change job state through `setStatus` so `history` records who did what
- ALWAYS validate input at the boundary: `validateBrief`, `validateBrand`, `validateSource`, `validateScript`
- ALWAYS keep director runs and asset generation capped by `config/studio.json` → `director` (max jobs per run, minutes per job, runs per day) and `director.api` (turns and tokens per job, calls per day, timeouts, bytes, prepare rounds, page fetches per job) and `generate` (requests per day and per month: `maxImagesPerDay`, `maxImagesPerMonth`, `maxVideosPerDay`, `maxVideosPerMonth`, `maxRefreshesPerDay`; timeout, bytes)
- ALWAYS add or update a `tests/*.test.mjs` case when you change engine validation, locks, timing or a template contract
- ALWAYS run the tests a change can affect while you work (`npm run test:changed`: `tests/run.mjs` picks them from the changed functions and their callers, `--list` shows why), and the full `npm test` before calling a change done or committing
- ALWAYS describe a new template with `beats.json` (sequence, fields, limits, enums, defaults) and test it through `tests/templates.test.mjs`
- ALWAYS draw template sizes in units of a 1080 short side via `geometry(size).px()` (side padding via `padX()`) so every format (16:9, 1:1, 9:16, 4:5, 2:3, 21:9) shares one layout
- ALWAYS mark text that must fit the safe area with `data-lint` so `lintInPage` checks it
- ALWAYS keep user-facing strings short, plain English and specific about the fix ("Approve the storyboard first")
- ALWAYS log an AI-typed error you caught (hallucinated API, confident-but-wrong, convention violation) with `node .claude/scripts/append-ai-failure.js`
<!-- END:ALWAYS -->

## Code Quality (same change, not a later cleanup)
- Standard library before hand-rolling or adding a dependency (`node:fs`, `node:path`, `URL`, `node:test`)
- No dead code: nothing exported without a real consumer; remove imports the change made unused
- A literal used 2+ times becomes a named constant; caps live in `config/studio.json`
- Simplify after green: re-read the diff for a shorter form and stale comments
- Rules enforced in two places stay in sync: `beats.json` limits ↔ renderer layout, server validation ↔ UI editor

## Prose Voice
Applies to prose you generate: chat replies, docs, plan files, commit bodies. Source of truth: `.claude/output-styles/motion-studio.md` § "Prose voice". Short sentences, no filler, take a position and cite a real file or number. Check with `node .ai/scripts/prose-audit.js <file>`.

