Read these before writing code. Do not grep for files that file-index lists.

## Scope of a Change
The request sets the scope. Implement every behaviour asked for, completely; anything else is a follow-up you report.
- A pre-existing bug the task does not mention is a follow-up, unless the requested behaviour cannot work without it.
- Where the task is ambiguous, implement the reading the wording and code most directly support, and state the assumption.
- Scratch scripts need not be kept. Commit tests where the repo keeps tests for that kind of change (`tests/*.test.mjs`).

## Editing Files (token cost)
Prefer a targeted edit over rewriting a whole file. Reserve rewrites for short files or when most of the file changes.

## Update Propagation (MANDATORY)
When a rule, convention, pattern or workflow changes, update the affected agents and skills in the same change:
1. Edit `.ai/docs/conventions.md` (source of truth)
2. `node .claude/scripts/generate-mirrors.js`
3. Update affected `.claude/agents/*.md`, `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md`, `.cursor/agents/*.md`, `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`
4. Verify: `node .claude/scripts/check-propagation.js`
Full details: `.ai/docs/kit-process.md` → "Mandatory Update Propagation".
